&piece title="Swing: the long and the short" tags="tutorial, rhythm" tier=4 label="Eighths played long and short: a swing clock, and the same feel from swing= on the bar." about=&out
&clockNote label="&swing is a clock of its own: scan(2 1), a long step and a short, two to a beat. What steps with it swings." about=&swing
&swingNote label="swing=.67 on a bar says the same: of each pair of steps, the second comes two thirds of the way through. beat=2: two of the bar's steps make a beat." about=&bar2
&bar scan(1 1 1 1) step=free(moderato)
&swing scan(2 1) step=&bar                       # long, short: a pair a beat
&bar2 1!8 step=free(moderato) beat=2 swing=.67   # the same, written on the bar

&walk over=scale(major, G) step=&bar 0 2 4 5 7 5 4 2
&ride step=&swing 12!3 ~ 12!3 ~
&comp over=scale(major, G) step=&bar2 ~ [2,4,6] ~!3 [2,4,6] ~ [2,4,6]

&bass s=sine loop=G2 env=&(map=adsr .01 .4 .5 .1)
&cymbal s=white hpf=7000 env=&(map=adsr 0 .2 0 .1)
&piano s=tri loop=G3 env=&(map=adsr .005 .4 .2 .2)
&out map=sample postgain=1.88 [&walk * &bass * .5, &ride * &cymbal * .1, &comp * &piano * .15]
